.TH ONE-MK 1 "" "one-mk" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
one-mk, one-mk-tray, one-mk-app \- share one mouse and keyboard between computers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B one-mk
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.br
.B one-mk-tray
[\fB\-\-home\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-start\-daemon\fR]
.br
.B one-mk-app
[\fB\-\-home\fR \fIDIR\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B one-mk
moves the mouse and keyboard to the next computer when the pointer crosses the edge of the screen, and shares
the clipboard and files. \fBone-mk-tray\fR is an optional tray icon and \fBone-mk-app\fR is the settings window.
.PP
Typical use, on every computer:
.PP
.nf
one-mk install    # start at login
one-mk pair       # pair with another computer (run it on both)
.fi
.PP
\fBone-mk integrate\fR adds "Send to <computer>" to the file manager menu.
.SH OPTIONS AND COMMANDS
Run \fBone-mk \-\-help\fR for the list of commands and \fBone-mk help\fR \fICOMMAND\fR for one command.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/one-mk
Identity key and paired computers.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/user/one-mk.service
systemd user service: \fBsystemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now one-mk\fR (or run \fBone-mk install\fR).
.SH SEE ALSO
.I https://github.com/samer2373/one-mk
